-- ============================================================================
-- DC23 - ReservoirCalc Pro EXPERT (advanced tier) goes deep.
--
-- Flips (reservoircalc, advanced) onto the DC1 deep path by inserting its ACTIVE
-- academy_course_structures row, generated from the repo manifest
-- src/content/courses/reservoircalc/advanced/manifest.json (emitted by a
-- generator, not hand-typed), and seeding the six module quiz banks plus the
-- final exam. Answer keys live only here and in the table.
--
-- COMPLETES THE RESERVOIRCALC PRO LADDER at all three tiers, the sixth app to
-- finish after petrophysics, welldata, wellcorrelation, seismolord and mapping.
--
-- Every numeric item traces to the reservoircalc teaching oracle and reproduces
-- the live NG7 Expert capstone answer key: the constant porosity is replaced by a
-- grid populated from the six well values with the population engine and the
-- volumetrics rerun at the 1560 m contact, giving trend porosity at prospect P-1
-- 0.20714187889686578, mean over the oil nodes 0.20936760570720417, pore volume
-- 3.7558468705687864e6 m3, HCPV 2.4413004882563025e6 m3, STOIIP 12.79607650919541
-- MMstb and an uplift of 0.656868401698647 MMstb over the constant booking. The
-- same pipeline src/lib/reservoircalcTeaching.js drives and propertyLab.test.js
-- pins.
--
-- Tier note: the Associate tier (DC9) owns the chain and forward-quoted this
-- tier's headline; the Professional tier (DC22) owns the partition, which this
-- tier deliberately sets aside so that the property model is the only change.
-- This tier owns what is inside the headline. populate('trend') is a LEAST
-- SQUARES PLANE (0.24107144716926077 - 2.043684820796242e-5 x - 7.691319622844493e-7
-- y), so it honours NO well: it misses four of the six by more than 8 pct of the
-- measured value, worst 0.019309143835140874 at Ekene-3, and the residuals sum to
-- zero because the model carries an intercept. Three defensible means exist and
-- differ: the arithmetic well mean 0.20666666666666667, the node mean over the 169
-- oil cells 0.20936760570720417 (graded), and the volume weighted mean
-- 0.21082226429530276 which is pore over net and the only one the booking can use.
-- The geometry is untouched (169 cells, 22.26903564453125e6 m3 gross and
-- 17.81522878109259e6 m3 net are identical to the constant run) and the chain
-- diverges only at the pore step, so the whole model delivers one ratio,
-- 1.0541113057690301. THE DECOMPOSITION is the centrepiece: booking at the
-- arithmetic well mean gives 12.543847985822008 MMstb, so 0.404639878325245 of the
-- headline uplift is only a better constant and just 0.252228523373402 is spatial.
-- The sign is positive because the modelled porosity correlates with oil column at
-- +0.46242377439477966 over the oil cells.
--
-- Bank standard: measured on the length RANK of the correct option and checked for
-- cyclic key sequences, answer-index skew and within-pool near-duplicates before
-- seeding. Across the 132 questions the correct option is longest in 23 pct and
-- shortest in 24 pct.
--
-- Enrollment grandfathering: enforced_from defaults to now() on first insert; the
-- ON CONFLICT update deliberately leaves enforced_from unchanged on re-seeds.
--
-- Ladder note: an ADVANCED enrollment needs an unrevoked PROFESSIONAL
-- certification on the SAME app, so the dry-run probes back-stop a reservoircalc
-- professional cert in-transaction, and probes confirm BOTH tiers below
-- (reservoircalc beginner and reservoircalc intermediate) are left undisturbed at
-- 132 questions each.
--
-- NO DDL. Data only.
-- ============================================================================

values ('reservoircalc', 'advanced', '{"modules":[{"key":"m01-from-a-constant-to-a-grid","title":"From a Constant to a Grid","lesson_keys":["l01-what-this-tier-adds","l02-the-engine-was-always-ready","l03-the-six-well-porosities","l04-the-property-panel-map"]},{"key":"m02-the-trend-plane","title":"The Trend Plane","lesson_keys":["l01-three-ways-to-fill-a-grid","l02-what-a-least-squares-plane-is","l03-the-ekene-plane","l04-the-model-honours-no-well","l05-outside-the-wells"]},{"key":"m03-three-means","title":"Three Means","lesson_keys":["l01-an-average-is-no-longer-one-number","l02-the-arithmetic-well-mean","l03-the-node-mean-over-the-oil","l04-the-volume-weighted-mean","l05-which-mean-belongs-in-the-booking"]},{"key":"m04-what-the-model-buys","title":"What the Property Model Buys","lesson_keys":["l01-the-chain-diverges-at-the-pore-step","l02-the-uplift-is-one-ratio","l03-the-decomposition","l04-why-the-sign-is-positive","l05-the-number-in-proportion"]},{"key":"m05-the-limits-of-a-property-model","title":"The Limits of a Property Model","lesson_keys":["l01-two-properties-still-constant","l02-a-plane-is-a-strong-assumption","l03-a-method-that-honours-the-data","l04-the-well-the-map-could-not-report","l05-invented-detail"]},{"key":"m06-the-property-workflow","title":"The Property Workflow","lesson_keys":["l01-the-workflow-end-to-end","l02-quality-control","l03-the-capstone-walkthrough","l04-the-top-of-the-ladder"]}]}'::jsonb, 1)
